fans of the Marvel Cinematic Universe  got an early Christmas present when it  was announced in December 17 that Disney  would be acquiring a large portion of  Fox including the movie rights did the  x-men and the Fantastic Four with the  dream of a unified MCU finally on the  verge of becoming reality let's look at  all the best Marvel characters Disney is  getting from Fox Wolverine and the x-men  obviously the biggest question for fans  is what Marvel will do with Fox's  massive x-men franchise which is so far  produced three solo Wolverine films as  well as six x-men movies with a seventh  on the way in 2018 merging the x-men  franchise with the MCU would be a  massive undertaking should they recast  the roles and reboot the x-men entirely  or should they use the x-men franchises  frequent timeline shifts and read cons  to simply add the whole existing x-men  universe to the MCU if you thought  understanding the x-men films was  difficult before get ready for a wild  ride will Wolverine make the leap  Michael the Fantastic Four even though  they've appeared in only four movies to  date the Fantastic Four have never truly  worked on screen so for fans the most  exciting thing about the Disney Fox  merger is the possibility that we'll  finally get a good Fantastic Four movie  so far they've been well two guys a girl  and the thing that nobody wanted at  their heart the Fantastic Four  aren't superheroes they're adventurers  using science and superpowers to explore  other dimensions other realities and the  unknown depths of our universe films  like Thor the guardians of the galaxy  and Doctor Strange have introduced some  of the weirder corners of the MCU to  fans but it's the Fantastic Four who are  best designed to explore them we can't  wait Galactus  the biggest and baddest villain in the  Marvel Universe Galactus literally eats  planets for breakfast so fans were  terribly disappointed when Fox wasted  him in Fantastic Four rise of the Silver  Surfer by showing him as just an angry  space cloud instead of the world  devouring giant from the comics  of course the lactis never goes anywhere  alone and his coming to disney also  means that Marvel Studios has the right  suit all his heralds not just the Silver  Surfer  but others including the loyal Airwalker  the villainous morg  the adventurous Nova and the ambitious  Terrax once Thanos is through as a  threat don't be surprised if you start  hearing rumblings of Galactus as the  next big bad worthy of a franchise  spanning team-up Silver Surfer speaking  of The Sentinel of the spaceways the  Silver Surfer didn't exactly blow people  away when he made his big screen debut  in 2006 but his tragic story of  sacrifice and loss where he gives up his  freedom to save humanity is timeless add  in his iconic design and you have a  character with the potential to be a  breakout star in the MCU Deadpool fans  have to be salivating at the idea of  Deadpool joining the Marvel Cinematic  Universe some of the funniest jokes in  the surprise 2016 smash hit film  involved Ryan Reynolds playing off the  straight-laced x-men it's a big house  it's funny that I only ever see two of  you it's almost like the studio couldn't  afford another x-men now imagine what  he'll do when he runs into characters  like Doctor Strange Tony Stark or even  spider-man we can't wait to hear the  one-liners fly Legion it's safe to say  that nobody outside of hardcore comic  book fans had ever heard of the  character Legion until FX debuted the  critically acclaimed TV series starring  Downton Abbey's Dan Stevens now though  the character provides some intriguing  possibilities thanks to his connection  to the x-men universe through deadbeat  dad Professor Xavier and his  reality-warping powers could be a handy  way to easily ride him into any  franchise the honchos at marvel studios  once the possibilities are endless and  intriguing the new mutants the next  generation of students at Charles  Xavier's school for gifted cannon fodder  the new mutants are finally coming  the big scream in 2018 with a horror  tinge adaptation of the classic demon  bear storyline while the film only  focuses on a handful of characters  including magic Wolfsbane cannonball  sunspot and Mirage the new mutants  lineup also includes a number of other  fan favorites like karma warlock and  magma traditionally aimed at a slightly  younger demographic than x-men it will  be interesting to see how or if the new  mutants fit into the Marvel Cinematic  Universe Alpha Flight in February 2017  x-men producers Simon Kinberg made  reference to an in the works ex flight  movie which many took to be referring to  a new version of the never before  adapted team alpha flight formed by the  Canadian government with the help of  Wolverine alpha flight has strong ties  to the x-men universe while maintaining  its own identity thanks to unique and  offbeat characters like shaman puck  Northstar Snowbird and Sasquatch in a  world where guardians of the galaxy have  become household names with a little  tender loving care for Marvel Studios  Alpha Flight could become the next big  thing Doctor Doom one of the most  awesome developments from the Disney Fox  deal doesn't involve the heroes it  brings to the MCU but rather the  villains and no Marvel Comics villain is  more thoroughly iconic than Doctor Doom  while doom is mostly known for his  eternal rivalry with the Fantastic Four  the ruler of Latveria has also gone  toe-to-toe with just about everyone else  in the MCU so far fans haven't been  thrilled with the way he's been  portrayed in the Fox movies so a doom  that actually lives up to the characters  great legacy in the comics would be a  very welcome change and if you think  otherwise Kang the Conqueror he's  considered to be the Avengers ultimate  arch enemy battling Earth's Mightiest  Heroes dozens of times over the decades  but thanks to a quirk in their licensing  deal the movie rights for Kang were  apparently shipped over to Fox along  with Fantastic Four meaning The Avengers  were left without their greatest foe now  though it's possible that the  time-traveling warlord Kang who has  conquered countless empires throughout  history  we'll finally get to set his sights on  the 21st century MCU all we can say is  it's about time thanks for watching  click the looper icon to subscribe to  our YouTube channel plus check out all  this cool stuff we know you love to  [Music]
 

